Subject: [PATCH] fix: unwrapped script leaks + duplicate </body></html> in RCM
 OS module chain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Scoped fully to the 10 files wired into tsm-rcm-os.html's Connected
Modules (compliance.html, finops-operations.html, finops-accounting.html,
finops-scenarios.html, finance-index.html, finops-showcase-v1.html,
supplier-vendor-situation-room.html, logistics-situation-room.html,
tsm-rcm-os.html, tsm-rcm-os-howto.html). 6 of the 10 were already clean.

compliance.html (deeper fix beyond the earlier tsmAI patch):
- 5 separate regions of raw JS were rendering as visible text on the
  page because they were pasted in without a wrapping <script> tag:
  the BNCA node reporter IIFE, a duplicate/dead showTab() + stub
  aiAnalyzeAlerts() pair, and the License & Renewal / Audit Workspace
  helper functions.
- The duplicate showTab()/aiAnalyzeAlerts() were REMOVED rather than
  wrapped: they targeted a .tab-content class that doesn't exist
  anywhere in this file (real markup uses .tab-pane) and a plain-fetch
  stub with no spinner/modal, respectively. Wrapping them as-is would
  have made them execute last and silently override the real, working
  showTab() (line 1656) and aiAnalyzeAlerts() (line 1945).
- The file also had a duplicate </body></html> pair: trailing
  TSM_AUTONOMY_STANDARDIZED + war-room-relay code had been appended
  after the real closing tags with its own (invalid) closing tags.
  Merged into one properly wrapped <script> block before the single
  real </body></html>.

finops-operations.html, finops-accounting.html, finops-scenarios.html:
- Same duplicate </body></html> pattern as compliance.html (trailing
  TSM_AUTONOMY_STANDARDIZED + war-room-relay fix appended post-close).
  finops-accounting.html and finops-scenarios.html were missing a
  final closing tag entirely. Fixed identically: content wrapped in
  one <script> block, moved before a single closing </body></html>.
- Checked all three for duplicate function/variable names introduced
  by the fix — none found.

Verified via a script-tag balance walker (accounting for same-line
close-then-reopen patterns) across all 10 files: zero unwrapped
regions, exactly one <body>/<html> close each.

Left the other ~430 affected files elsewhere in the repo untouched
per scope — same underlying pattern exists there but is out of scope
for this pass.
